      "assessment": "A reviewed numeric-algorithm mapping is possible; immutable canonical names/proof signers and authenticated lifetime history are not supplied by a raw key hash or verified flag. Revocation removes enumeration entries; separate KEM mutation is not the addition of an immutable named entry.",
      "required_evidence": [
        {
          "id": "named-key-history",
          "status": "EVIDENCE_REQUIRED",
          "requirement": "Establish immutable names, algorithms, public material/proofs/optional expiry, authoritative retained revoked entries and no name/material reuse."
        },
        {
          "id": "key-write-lifecycle",
          "status": "EVIDENCE_REQUIRED",
          "requirement": "Enforce active-only additions, bounded lifetime entries and revocation with atomic deactivation when the last usable signing key is lost, rather than a raw key count."
        },
        {
          "id": "role-and-kem-selection",
          "status": "EVIDENCE_REQUIRED",
          "requirement": "Keep message signing and X25519 KEM separate; select the first eligible named KEM entry without mutating or substituting in-flight authority."
        }
